<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
		The only iCloud location a sandboxed iOS app can reach is a container
		it owns, which is why sync on the phone is this container or nothing.
		`URLForUbiquityContainerIdentifier` returns nil without these three
		keys, and the container must also be registered to the team and named
		in the provisioning profile. That portal half was done on 2026-08-06
		and checked by decoding the profile, not by reading Xcode's UI.

		Two traps on the way there, both cheap to fall into twice. The App ID's
		iCloud capability defaults to "Compatible with Xcode 5", a 2014 mode
		that signs ubiquity-container-identifiers alone and emits neither of
		the other two keys — the fix is the radio button labelled "Include
		CloudKit support", which despite the name only selects the modern
		entitlement set and obliges nobody to use CloudKit. And the Signing &
		Capabilities pane renders *this file*, not the portal, so a ticked
		container there is not evidence that Apple will grant one. The
		authority is the decoded .mobileprovision.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.icloud-container-identifiers</key>
	<array>
		<string>iCloud.com.klaragraff.lantern</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.ubiquity-container-identifiers</key>
	<array>
		<string>iCloud.com.klaragraff.lantern</string>
	</array>
	<!--
		Documents, not CloudKit. Lantern syncs a directory of files: an
		append-only JSONL log plus book and cover blobs. Nothing here wants a
		record database.

		Enabling iCloud from Xcode's UI also ticks Key-value storage and writes
		a ubiquity-kvstore-identifier key in here. Lantern keeps no key-value
		data in iCloud, so it gets removed again — an entitlement nothing
		claims is one more question at review time and one more capability a
		compromised build would inherit.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.icloud-services</key>
	<array>
		<string>CloudDocuments</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
